    body: '- Kingdom - the largest group, for example Animalia or Plantae\n- Phylum - in animals, Chordata contains all vertebrates\n- Class - Mammalia is marked by hair and mammary glands\n- Order - a subdivision of a class\n- Family - a subdivision of an order\n- Genus - the first word of the scientific name\n- Species - members can interbreed and produce fertile offspring\n- Binomial nomenclature: genus with a capital, species in lower case, as Escherichia coli\n- Linnaeus introduced binomial nomenclature\n- Five kingdoms often used: Animalia, Plantae, Fungi, Protista, Monera\n- Population: one species in one area at one time\n- Community: all the populations living together in an area\n- Ecosystem: the community plus the non-living surroundings'
